==============================================================================
'the same number every time I ask'
==============================================================================

Four differently-written queries for October revenue, run five times each.
Two read the aggregate, one reads the fact table, one goes all the way back to
the raw landed lines in the object store.  If the model is sound they cannot
disagree.

  agg, filtered on business_month                 56,359,195.92   all 5 runs identical
  agg, rolled up from store and category          56,359,195.92   all 5 runs identical
  fact table, joined to dim_date                  56,359,195.92   all 5 runs identical
  raw landed lines in the object store            56,359,195.92   all 5 runs identical

  finance, signed off 2024-11-09                  56,359,195.92

  all four routes agree : True
  agrees with finance   : True
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
and the number the old spreadsheet gives
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  sum of every row in October's files :     122,501,668.06
  revenue                             :      56,359,195.92
  inflation                           :               2.17x

  That is the surprisingly healthy October.  It is TENDER -- the bill
  total, written into the same file as another row -- plus the GST.

